chains:
We need to simplify the expression (4+3c)/7 + 2 into a single fraction. Write 2 as 2 * (7/7) = 14/7. So sum = (4+3c)/7 + 14/7 = (4+3c + 14)/7 = (18 + 3c)/7. We can factor 3: (3(6 + c))/7. So final answer: \frac{3(6 + c)}{7}. Or \frac{3c+18}{7}. So answer in box.

Thus final answer: \boxed{\frac{3c+18}{7}}.
\frac{4+3c}{7}+2
= \frac{4+3c}{7}+\frac{2\cdot7}{7}
= \frac{4+3c+14}{7}
= \frac{18+3c}{7}
= \frac{3(6+c)}{7}


\[
\boxed{\dfrac{3c+18}{7}}
\]

